                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              denotes is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+differential"} de Rham differential
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Up to possibly a global sign, it does not matter whether
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_\mu
              in
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FeynmanAmplitudedRadiativeDalitzDecay"} (1)
              or
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FeynmanAmplitudedSemileptonicDalitzDecay"} (3)
              is taken to be the wave vector of the external photon/vector meson (as stated for instance in
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#YiaSang09"} Yia-Sang 09, (9)
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#FLQY12"} FLQY 12
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "#GLMY19"} GLMY 19, (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_\mu
              of the scalar meson, and due to anti-symmetry of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levi-Civita+symbol"} Levi-Civita symbol
              this difference vanishes inside the above expression.
            %p
              Equivalently, in terms of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LagrangianDensityForSemileptonicDalitzDecay"} (4)
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+derivative"} total derivative
            .maruku-equation
